item.emergency_kit.description=Right click to equip Oxygen Gear and other essential items. Warning: One time use!
item.lunar_sapphire.description=Lunar Sapphires are the unit of currency when trading with Alien Villagers
tile.air_lock_frame.description=Air Lock Frames, when arranged in a portal-like formation, with a single block replaced with a controller, will function as a working air lock.
tile.aluminum_wire.alu_wire.description=Aluminum Wire is used to connect energy sources to energy consuming machines.
tile.aluminum_wire.alu_wire_heavy.description=Heavy Aluminum Wire is used to connect energy sources to energy consuming machines. Its higher capacity boosts efficiency for Tier 2 machines.
tile.aluminum_wire.alu_wire_switch.description=Switchable Aluminum Wire connects like Aluminum Wire, unless switched OFF with a redstone signal.
tile.aluminum_wire.alu_wire_switch_heavy.description=Switchable Heavy Aluminum Wire connects like Heavy Aluminum Wire, unless switched OFF with a redstone signal.
tile.arclamp.description=Arc Lamps are used to provide strong light to a large area, also causing most mobs to flee.
tile.buggy_pad.description=Fueling Pads will allow a buggy on the pad to be refueled by an attached Fuel Loaders if set up in a 3x3 square.  Cannot be used to launch rockets!
tile.cargo_loader.description=Cargo Loaders will pass blocks and items onto Rockets and other vehicles with cargo space. Must be attached to Landing/Fueling pad.
tile.cargo_unloader.description=Cargo Unloaders will extract blocks and items from Rockets and other vehicles with cargo space. Must be attached to Landing/Fueling pad.
tile.cheese.description=Cheese Blocks are created from the cheeses of the Moon, place-able and edible.
tile.circuit_fabricator.description=Circuit Fabricator will process basic materials into silicon wafers, used for advanced machines.
tile.coal_generator.description=Coal Generator will burn coal (or a Block of Coal) for energy. The simplest but least efficient energy production method.
tile.collector.description=Oxygen Collector will store oxygen collected from leaves in the surrounding area.
tile.compressor.description=Compressor will process ingots into their compressed equivalents. The most essential machine in Galacticraft!
tile.compressor_electric.description=Electric Compressor will process ingots into their compressed equivalents. Compresses two at a time, making it more effective than its predecessor.
tile.compressor_advanced.description=A faster version of the Electric Compressor.  Rapidly processes ingots into their compressed equivalents.
tile.deconstructor.description=The Deconstructor will take apart your old rockets and other items, returning any salvageable materials.
tile.dishbase.description=The Communications Dish can track the position of space stations and receive communications from your remote space bases.
tile.distributor.description=Oxygen Distributor will emit an oxygen bubble outwards from the center block, using internal tank. This allows safe breathing inside the bubble.
tile.electric_furnace_tier1.description=Electric Furnace is used as a faster alternative to traditional coal furnaces.
tile.electric_furnace_tier2.description=Electric Arc Furnace is used as a better and faster alternative to both traditional coal and electric furnaces: double output from ores!
tile.emergency_box.description=Place an Emergency Post close by your first landing place on a planet. Open to find Emergency Kit inside. Also repels mobs!
tile.enclosed.description=Sealable blocks should be used where air cannot pass, such as space base walls.
tile.energy_storage_module_tier1.description=Energy Storage Module is used to store large amounts of energy for later use.
tile.energy_storage_module_tier2.description=Energy Storage Cluster is used to store large amounts of energy for later use. Stores and outputs more energy than its predecessor.
tile.fallen_meteor.description=Fallen Meteors can be found in many planets/moons which have little or no atmosphere. Will drop Meteoric Iron when broken.
tile.fluid_pipe.description=Fluid Pipe will transfer liquid and gas from source to destination block. Use a Standard Wrench to switch modes.
tile.fluid_pipe_pull.description=Fluid Pipe will transfer liquid and gas from source to destination block. Use a Standard Wrench to switch modes.
tile.fluid_tank.description=Fluid Tanks will store liquids and gases for later use.
tile.fuel_loader.description=After being connected to a launch pad, a Fuel Loader will allow fuel to passed into the connected Rocket or other vehicle.
tile.glowstone_torch.description=Glowstone Torches are best used to light areas when there is no oxygen for wood torches to burn.
tile.landing_pad.description=Launch Pads will allow placement of Rockets if set up in a 3x3 square. Fuel Loaders, Cargo Loaders, and Launch Controllers can be attached.
tile.magnetic_table.description=Items placed won't fall off - it holds its inventory! Can shift-click items in. Hoppers can insert and remove items, it will attempt to automatically create the last recipe crafted.
tile.oxygen_compressor.description=Oxygen Compressor will load oxygen from internal storage into an oxygen tank.
tile.oxygen_decompressor.description=Oxygen Decompressor will unload oxygen into internal storage from an oxygen tank.
tile.oxygen_detector.description=Oxygen Detector will emit a redstone signal when surrounded by oxygen.
tile.oxygen_storage_module.description=Oxygen Storage Module is used to store large amounts of oxygen for later use.
tile.painter.description=Applies color to Vacuum Glass, Lighting Panels or other paintable objects. Use any block - or dye - to provide a fresh color!
tile.panel_lighting.description=Lighting panel for use in space! Wrench rotates it. To change the look: hold SNEAK while placing this against the chosen block.
tile.parachest.description=Parachests will fall from the sky after landing on certain planets/moons, such as Earth. Contains rocket, fuel, and cargo from previous launch.
tile.platform.description=Place 4 to form a platform. The platform lifts players to the next platform above or below. SNEAK = down : JUMP = up.
tile.refinery.description=Refinery will take an input of oil and energy, and output fuel used for rockets and vehicles.
tile.compact_workbench.description=Compact variant of the NASA Workbench.
tile.rocket_workbench.description=The NASA Workbench is used to create many advanced parts and vehicles. New schematics can be added as they are found.
tile.sealer.description=Oxygen Sealer will check for an enclosed space. If the space is enclosed, it will fill with breathable air.
tile.solar_adv.description=Advanced Solar Panels will collect energy from the sun, storing it for further use. Automatically adjusts panel angle for optimal energy collection.
tile.solar_basic.description=Basic Solar Panels will collect energy from the sun, storing it for further use. Collects most energy at mid-day (non-adjustable).
tile.space_glass.description=Vacuum sealed glass for your space bases. Paint the surround any color using a nearby Chromatic Applicator!
tile.space_glass.clear.description=Clear glass for great views of space, can also provide a clear view underwater.
tile.space_glass.strong.description=Strong and explosion-resistant glass. Made from Transparent Aluminum...
tile.spin_thruster.description=Spin Thrusters are used to make space stations rotate.
tile.telemetry.description=This gathers useful data from linked rockets, players and mobs. Best placed near to a Display Screen. Use a Frequency Module to establish data links.
tile.treasure_chest.description=Tier 1 Treasure Chests will generate in Moon Dungeons. They are unlockable after defeating the final boss.
tile.view_screen.description=Display screens add that final touch to your space base. Right-click changes the information shown.
